 "section_summary": "This section documents the progress and administration of Japan's postwar agricultural land reform, opening with an extensive SCAP sociological survey on rural attitudes toward agrarian reform, local land commissions, cooperatives, and inheritance customs. It further includes diplomatic reporting and SCAP materials on amendments to the Agricultural Land Adjustment Law regarding new land commission electoral categories. Finally, it contains official State Department and Japanese Ministry of Foreign Affairs correspondence transmitting writs and written notices of compulsory farmland purchase to Japanese absentee landowners residing in the United States and Venezuela.",
 "subfiles": [
  {
   "about": "A sociological survey report investigating Japanese farmers' attitudes toward village assessments, appeal procedures, land reform, tenancy contracts, local land commissions, agricultural cooperatives, inheritance customs, and information media.",
   "continues_previous": true,
   "date": "1949-05-20",
   "doc_type": "report",
   "end_page": 326,
   "from": "Civil Information and Education Section, GHQ, SCAP",
   "keywords": [
    "land reform",
    "survey",
    "land commissions",
    "agricultural cooperatives",
    "inheritance",
    "tenancy"
   ],
   "start_page": 293,
   "summary": "This survey examines opinions across thirteen rural villages regarding postwar agricultural conditions and policies. Farmers expressed broad satisfaction with the land reform program and trust in local commissions, while voicing concerns about village assessments and equal inheritance rules. The report also details rural reliance on agricultural cooperatives, local and national newspapers, and radio programs.",
   "title": "Attitudes of Farmers Toward Rural Problems",
   "to": ""
  },
  {
